   "translation": {
    "literal": "Āditya I satisfy. Soma I satisfy. Aṅgāraka I satisfy. Budha I satisfy. Bṛhaspati I satisfy. Śukra I satisfy. Śanaiścara I satisfy. Rāhu I satisfy. Ketu I satisfy.",
    "readable": "I offer water to the Sun, the Moon, Mars, Mercury, Jupiter, Venus, Saturn, Rāhu and Ketu."
   }
  }
 ],
 "meaning": "The nine grahas, the ‘seizers’ — the Sun, the Moon, the five visible planets, and the two nodes of the Moon’s path, Rāhu and Ketu — each receive water with ‘I satisfy (you)’. A tarpaṇa is an offering of water that ‘satisfies’ its recipient. The Smārta prayogas of the Āpastamba school offer it to the nine grahas and then to the twelve names of Viṣṇu; some Vaiṣṇava prayogas give only the twelve.",
 "in_the_rite": "Step tarpana, after the aikyānusandhāna and an ācamana, in all three services; water is poured from the hand for each name.",
 "notes": [
  {
   "label": "direct",
   "text": "Each line is the name in the accusative followed by tarpayāmi, ‘I satisfy’; the formula is the same for every recipient."
  },
  {
   "label": "historical",
   "text": "The witnesses differ only in M’s misprint अङ्गाकरं for अङ्गारकं (corrections.json)."
  }
 ],
